# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but every script and
# SQL file is executed inside a Linux container. Without the rules below, git
# hands out CRLF working copies on checkout and two things break:
#
#   *.sh      -> "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" the moment the
#                container tries to run it
#   Makefile  -> GNU Make passes the trailing \r to the shell and recipes fail
#                with "$'\r': command not found"
#
# Both failures appear only after a fresh clone, which is exactly when someone
# else (a marker, CI) runs the project. Pin everything to LF in the repository
# so the checkout is identical on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Called as executables inside the Linux container - CRLF is fatal, not cosmetic.
*.sh      text eol=lf
Makefile  text eol=lf

# Read by psql inside the container. CRLF runs, but the stray \r is copied into
# generated deliverables and breaks end-of-line matching in awk/sed.
*.sql     text eol=lf

*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf
*.puml    text eol=lf
